From 39cd0c75cd4021f6de3812dfbcecf1e0a65cb310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Changqing Li <changqing.li@windriver.com>
Date: Wed, 21 May 2025 20:21:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add url encoded username/password entry

With the latest two commits in git, refer [1][2], git prompt will url
encode the user and host, anspass should align with it, otherwise, the
saved entry will not match the git prompt, this will cause
"Authentication failed", and make wrlinux setup report error:
fatal: Authentication failed for 'https://xxx'
The saved user or password seems invalid, remove it and try again?

Since these two commits related to CVE fix, some low version of git also
possbile include these commits. And it is possible that some users
include these commits and some users don't include these commits,
anspass need to be compatibel with both cases, so we will insert both
encoded and unencoded username/password entry

[1] https://github.com/git/git/commit/7725b8100ffbbff2750ee4d61a0fcc1f53a086e8
[2] https://github.com/git/git/commit/c903985bf7e772e2d08275c1a95c8a55ab011577

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/Wind-River/anspass/pull/6]

Signed-off-by: Changqing Li <changqing.li@windriver.com>
